#
# Apply against the 8devices v3.4.11e vendor tree:
#   git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse \
#     -b v3.4.11e/openwrt-18.06-rtkmipsel-3.18 \
#     https://github.com/8devices/openwrt-8devices.git
#   cd openwrt-8devices && git sparse-checkout set package/kernel/rtl8192cd
#   patch -p1 < g3-rtl8192cd-4.14-port.patch
#
# ROOT CAUSE of the BSP_* symbol wall (measured via -E -dD on the real command
# line, not inferred): the driver's #include <bspchip.h> sites are UNREACHABLE
# DEAD CODE. 8192cd_osdep.c:168 gates them on CONFIG_RTL_819X, whose only
# self-define site (8192cd_cfg.h:168) is nested under #if !defined(__LINUX_2_6__)
# AND #if defined(CONFIG_RTL8196B|C|8198) - both false for 4.14/8197F. In the
# vendor SDK the symbol comes from the KERNEL's .config. No -I could ever help.
# 8192cd_hw.c uses a different dead gate, USE_RTL8186_SDK.
#
# Biggest single win: <asm/uaccess.h> -> <linux/uaccess.h> in 14 files (the
# correct post-3.4 spelling, which pulls linux/thread_info.h first) => 55 -> 101
# objects. Then two genuine vendor-rot fixes in Hal88XXTxDesc.c => 101 -> 116 + link.
#
